{
  "title": "Longest Quiet Stretch",
  "description": "## Task\n\nA sensor logs one noise level per minute. A minute is quiet when its level is at most `limit`. Find the length of the longest stretch of consecutive quiet minutes.\n\n## Input\n\n- `levels` — a list of non-negative integers. It may be empty.\n- `limit` — the highest level that still counts as quiet.\n\n## Output\n\nAn integer: the length of the longest run of consecutive entries that are all `<= limit`, or 0 if none.\n\n## Example\n\n```python\nlongest_quiet([3, 1, 2, 9, 1, 1, 1, 8], 3)  # returns 3\nlongest_quiet([9, 9], 3)  # returns 0\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 0 ≤ length of `levels` ≤ 10^5\n- 0 ≤ each level, `limit` ≤ 10^9\n",
  "signature": "def longest_quiet(levels: list[int], limit: int) -> int",
  "topic": "sliding window",
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "category": "two-pointers-windows",
